# Singleton Behaviour

Do not hand-roll `static Instance { get; private set; }` + duplicate `Awake` guards. Use the shared base that matches the assembly:

| Code lives in | Inherit | Assembly |
|---------------|---------|----------|
| Shared feature assemblies | `SharedSingletonBehaviour<T>` | `MonkeyTilt.Foundation` (namespace `MonkeyTilt.Shared`) |
| The game’s own assemblies | That game’s `SingletonBehaviour<T>` | The game’s runtime assembly (see its `AGENTS.md`) |

Same contract either way: throwing `Instance`, `HasInstance`, `TryGetInstance`, and a `ResetStatics` hook for the play-mode reset hub. Neither base calls `DontDestroyOnLoad` — lifetime is whatever placed the object (scene/prefab).

## Creating a new singleton

```csharp
// Shared feature
public class NetTraceWindow : SharedSingletonBehaviour<NetTraceWindow>
{
    public static new void ResetStatics() => SharedSingletonBehaviour<NetTraceWindow>.ResetStatics();

    protected override void OnSingletonAwake() { }
}

// Game assembly (parallel type, same shape)
public class SFXManager : SingletonBehaviour<SFXManager>
{
    public static new void ResetStatics() => SingletonBehaviour<SFXManager>.ResetStatics();

    protected override void OnSingletonAwake() { }
}
```

Register `T.ResetStatics()` in the project’s `PlayModeStaticReset` (see domain-reload-statics rule). Clear any static events in that override.

## Access rules — fail fast, never silently skip

`Instance` **throws** when no instance exists. Missing singletons are bugs, not optional dependencies.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — silently skips work when singleton is missing
if (GameFlow.Instance != null)
    GameFlow.Instance.StartMatch();
SFXManager.Instance?.Play(Sfx.Click);

// ✅ GOOD — throws immediately if misconfigured
GameFlow.Instance.StartMatch();
SFXManager.Instance.Play(Sfx.Click);
```

**Never** use on singleton `Instance` accessors:

- `?.` (null-conditional) or `??` fallback
- `if (X.Instance != null)` / `== null` before normal use
- `if (mgr == null) return` immediately after `var mgr = X.Instance`

## Allowed non-throwing APIs (narrow exceptions)

Only for bootstrap, lazy creation, or teardown — not everyday feature code:

| API | Use when |
|-----|----------|
| `HasInstance` | Guard before creating the singleton (`Ensure*`, auto-spawn) |
| `TryGetInstance(out var x)` | `OnDestroy` / unsubscribe when play mode may have already cleared the instance |

```csharp
// Bootstrap
if (SFXManager.HasInstance) return;
new GameObject("SFXManager").AddComponent<SFXManager>();

// Teardown
if (GameFlow.TryGetInstance(out var flow))
    flow.MatchEnded.RemoveListener(OnMatchEnded);
```

`while (mgr != null && ...)` on a **captured reference** in a coroutine is OK — that guards object destruction mid-coroutine, not singleton existence.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] Shared code uses `SharedSingletonBehaviour<T>`; game code uses the game’s `SingletonBehaviour<T>`
- [ ] `ResetStatics()` registered in `PlayModeStaticReset`
- [ ] No `?.`, `??`, or `Instance != null` guards on singleton access in feature code
- [ ] Lazy creation uses `HasInstance`; teardown uses `TryGetInstance`
